  "body": "Part of #1733.\n\nThe fix for #1733 adds the corner arc radius to the arc turns option of these kinds:\n\n- 2D Pocket\n- 2D Adaptive (Spiral method; the Trochoidal method refuses the option by name)\n- 2D Offset\n\nThese kinds do not have the option yet:\n\n- Slot. Open PR #1745 (issue 1731) changes Slot. Do this work after PR #1745 merges, so that the two PRs do not conflict.\n- Face.\n- 2D Contour. A contour follows the wall, so a rounded corner can leave material on an outside corner. Examine which corners can turn on an arc in the region the sharp pass cuts.\n\nUse the same parameters as the three kinds above: `blend_turns` and `blend_radius`. No radius means the tool radius. The bound and the refusal text are in `camcraft_motion::machining2d::corner_arc_radius` and in `crates/app/src/operation/types/sane.rs`.\n\nDone means:\n- Each kind that can round its corners safely has the option and the radius as operation parameters. The undoable parameter command and MCP `edit_operation` set them.\n- A toolpath test for each kind pins the corners as tangent arcs of the given radius, and pins that no arc cuts past the wall.\n- The default output of each kind does not change. No golden changes.\n- A kind that cannot round its corners safely is named in the PR with the reason.\n",
